    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Adam Brewer - Senior Full-Stack Engineer">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Frontend architecture, APIs and AWS serverless. Creator of Mapbox TUI and Rust contributor to Strata. TypeScript, React, Next.js, GraphQL and Go.">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://brewerlogic.com/assets/img/logo-og.png">

    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
    {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Adam Brewer",
        "description": "Senior full-stack engineer specialising in frontend architecture and production SaaS delivery, with AWS serverless experience and merged Rust contributions to Strata.",
        "jobTitle": "Senior Full-Stack Engineer",
        "url": "https://brewerlogic.com",
        "sameAs": [
            "https://github.com/adamcbrewer",
            "https://linkedin.com/in/adamcbrewer"
        ],
        "knowsAbout": ["GraphQL", "Rust", "Go", "AWS", "TypeScript", "React", "Next.js", "Frontend Architecture", "JavaScript", "Node.js", "Design Systems", "Accessibility", "React Native", "Ionic", "MongoDB", "PostgreSQL", "Docker", "CI/CD", "AI-assisted Engineering"],
        "email": "adam@brewerlogic.com"
    }
    </script>

    <SiteFonts />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/assets/img/bl-logo.svg">
    <script is:inline>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/palette.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/navigation.css">
    <script is:inline src="/assets/js/navigation.js" defer></script>

</head>
<body>
    <a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

    <div class="grid-lines" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </div>

    <SiteHeader />

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">

        <section class="hero">
            <div class="hero__name-bg" aria-hidden="true">ADAM<br>BREWER</div>
            <div class="hero__content">
                <h1 class="hero__name reveal reveal--delay-1">Adam<br>Brewer</h1>
                <h2 class="hero__tagline reveal reveal--delay-2">Senior engineer</h2>
                <p class="hero__tagline-sub reveal reveal--delay-3">TypeScript / React / Next.js / GraphQL / Rust / Go / AWS</p>
                <p class="hero__description reveal reveal--delay-3">
                    15+ years delivering fintech, SaaS and design-system products.
                    Co-founder of Paper Trails (<a href="https://papertrails.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">papertrails.io</a>),
                    creator of <a href="https://github.com/adamcbrewer/mapbox-tui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mapbox TUI</a> and contributor to <a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Strata</a>.
                </p>
                <div class="hero__cta reveal reveal--delay-4">
                    <a href="/Adam-Brewer-Senior-Full-Stack-Engineer-CV.pdf" class="btn btn--primary" download>Download CV</a>
                    <a href="#work" class="btn btn--secondary">See my work</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <span class="hero__marker" aria-hidden="true">Portfolio / 2026</span>
        </section>

        <div class="accent-strip" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <section id="about" class="section">
            <span class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">About</span>
            <div class="section__number-bg" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
            <div class="section__inner">
                <h2 class="section__title reveal">
                    <span>01 - About</span>
                    What I Do
                </h2>
                <div class="about__grid">
                    <div class="about__text reveal reveal--delay-1">
                        <p>
                            I'm a full-stack engineer building web and mobile apps with TypeScript, React, Next.js and Node.js. I work
                            across the whole stack and particularly enjoy spending time on the frontend. I also work with GraphQL, Rust,
                            Go and AWS.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            At Quilter, I was part of the engineering team that took the web and mobile apps from proof of concept to
                            production within nine months. I worked closely with product, design, backend and QA teams, and helped
                            maintain the apps across multiple deployments in the following years.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I co-founded <a href="https://papertrails.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paper Trails</a> and
                            built and maintained the entire stack end to end. That includes turning route data into prints, taking
                            payments, deployment and production support.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I built
                            <a href="https://github.com/adamcbrewer/mapbox-tui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mapbox TUI</a>, a Go app for exploring maps and planning journeys in the terminal. It can play back activities, read files
                            offline and connect to AI agents through a local MCP server. I also contribute to
                            <a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Strata</a>, a Rust/GTK4
                            file manager for Linux. My work there includes sandboxed file previews, keyboard controls for tabs and fixes
                            for handling multiple windows.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I use AI daily for coding, technical reviews, debugging and fixing build and deployment pipelines. Agentic
                            workflows are a big part of how I work, and I'm building my own agent harnesses and software factory systems
                            to automate more of that work.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            At Meshii, I led the Polygon and Alchemy integration through a private pilot.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Before software, I was an aircraft technician in the British Army, maintaining military helicopters.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="skills reveal reveal--delay-2">
                        <p class="skills__heading">Core expertise</p>
                        <ul class="skills__list">
                            <li>GraphQL / REST APIs</li>
                            <li>Rust / GTK4</li>
                            <li>Go</li>
                            <li>AWS / Serverless</li>
                            <li>TypeScript / JavaScript</li>
                            <li>React / Next.js</li>
                            <li>Node.js / Server Actions</li>
                            <li>Frontend Architecture</li>
                            <li>Design Systems / Storybook</li>
                            <li>WCAG Accessibility</li>
                            <li>MongoDB / PostgreSQL</li>
                            <li>Jest / Playwright</li>
                            <li>Docker / CI/CD</li>
                            <li>AI-assisted Engineering</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cross-grid" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5">
                    <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="100" y2="100"/><line x1="100" y1="0" x2="0" y2="100"/>
                    <line x1="50" y1="0" x2="50" y2="100"/><line x1="0" y1="50" x2="100" y2="50"/>
                </svg>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="work" class="section">
            <span class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">Projects</span>
            <div class="section__number-bg" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
            <div class="section__inner">
                <h2 class="section__title reveal">
                    <span>02 - Work</span>
                    Featured<br>Projects
                </h2>
                <div class="projects">
                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Enterprise Fintech</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">Quilter</h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                Portfolio-planning platform for financial advisers. <strong>My contribution:</strong> I provided frontend
                                technical leadership, created the shared component architecture, and standardised server and complex
                                form state across Next.js web and Ionic React/Capacitor mobile clients. The platform reached production
                                within nine months and supported multiple subsequent releases. Client work is confidential.
                            </p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>React</li>
                                <li>Next.js</li>
                                <li>Ionic React</li>
                                <li>Capacitor</li>
                                <li>TypeScript</li>
                                <li>TanStack Query</li>
                                <li>Playwright</li>
                                <li>Azure</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Co-founded SaaS</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">
                                <a href="https://papertrails.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                    Paper Trails
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
                                </a>
                            </h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                A production platform that has fulfilled thousands of personalised print orders worldwide.
                                <strong>My contribution:</strong> As solo technical co-founder, I migrated the Laravel application to
                                Next.js and built the geospatial pipeline from Strava/GPX/FIT ingestion and Mapbox composition through
                                print rendering, Stripe commerce and Prodigi fulfilment.
                            </p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>React</li>
                                <li>Next.js</li>
                                <li>TypeScript</li>
                                <li>MongoDB</li>
                                <li>Mapbox</li>
                                <li>Stripe</li>
                                <li>Playwright</li>
                                <li>DigitalOcean</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal" id="mapbox-tui">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Open Source / Go</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">
                                <a href="https://github.com/adamcbrewer/mapbox-tui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                    Mapbox TUI
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
                                </a>
                            </h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">I created this Go terminal map explorer and journey planner.</p>
                            <ul class="project__desc project__features">
                                <li><strong>Agent remote control:</strong> Built CLI/MCP control of a running map: move the camera, edit journeys, manage imports and playback, and save or reopen workspaces.</li>
                                <li><strong>Journey planning:</strong> Mapbox walking, cycling and driving routes, editable waypoints and shareable commands to reopen plans.</li>
                                <li><strong>Activity exploration:</strong> Offline GPX, FIT, TCX and KML inspection, timed playback and elevation-profile comparisons across multiple files.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>Go</li>
                                <li>Mapbox</li>
                                <li>Terminal UI</li>
                                <li>Geospatial Data</li>
                                <li>MCP</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Open Source / Rust</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">
                                <a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                    Strata
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
                                </a>
                            </h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">My merged contributions to this Rust/GTK4 Linux file manager:</p>
                            <ul class="project__desc project__features">
                                <li><strong>Mesh previews:</strong> Added four on-demand camera views, triangle-count badges and cached renders for STL and single-part 3MF models. (<a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/1644" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1644</a>)</li>
                                <li><strong>Sandboxed previews:</strong> Added 3D-model rendering and ebook covers with bounded parsing and regression tests. (<a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/1276" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1276</a>, <a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/1325" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1325</a>)</li>
                                <li><strong>Navigation and state:</strong> Shipped keyboard tab controls and fixed multi-window bookmark cleanup. (<a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/1506" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1506</a>, <a href="https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/1373" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1373</a>)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>Rust</li>
                                <li>GTK4</li>
                                <li>Linux</li>
                                <li>Sandboxed Previews</li>
                                <li>Regression Testing</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">05</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Design System</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">
                                <a href="https://design-system.economist.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                    The Economist
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
                                </a>
                            </h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                React design system used across The Economist's digital products. <strong>My contribution:</strong>
                                I extended the tested component library and built its public Gatsby/MDX style-guide platform, including
                                generated component documentation, accessible patterns and visual-regression testing.
                            </p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>React</li>
                                <li>Gatsby</li>
                                <li>MDX</li>
                                <li>Storybook</li>
                                <li>Jest</li>
                                <li>Accessibility</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">06</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Mobile and Digital Rewards</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">Meshii WiFi</h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                Private-pilot application testing rewards for decentralised WiFi participation on Polygon's Mumbai test network.
                                <strong>My contribution:</strong> I led three developers, designed the React Native/Expo and AWS
                                serverless architecture, and integrated Alchemy test transactions with signed notifications that updated their status.
                            </p>
                            <p class="project__desc"><a href="/case-studies/meshii/">Read the architecture case study</a></p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>React Native</li>
                                <li>Expo</li>
                                <li>TypeScript</li>
                                <li>AWS Lambda</li>
                                <li>PostgreSQL</li>
                                <li>Polygon</li>
                                <li>Alchemy</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">07</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Selected Enterprise Work</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">Apple / Google</h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                <strong>My contribution:</strong> I modernised and supported a business-critical internal application
                                for Apple, with further details confidential. At Toaster, I built Google Play Policy guidance with
                                Polymer/Web Components and an interactive, touch-enabled Search Indonesia campaign.
                            </p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>React</li>
                                <li>TypeScript</li>
                                <li>Polymer</li>
                                <li>Web Components</li>
                                <li>Material Design</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="project reveal">
                        <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">08</div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="project__overline">Engineering Practice</p>
                            <h3 class="project__name">Human-Led, AI-Assisted Delivery</h3>
                            <p class="project__desc">
                                A structured way to use AI for production work without handing over engineering decisions.
                                <strong>My contribution:</strong> I set up reusable instructions and project context for OpenCode and
                                Claude Code. I diagnose the problem, design the solution and write the plan before AI drafts code,
                                tests and review. I then review, simplify and check the result. This approach supported my solo Paper
                                Trails migration from Laravel to Next.js and made wider automated testing practical.
                            </p>
                            <p class="project__desc"><a href="/case-studies/ai-engineering/">Read the Paper Trails production incident case study</a></p>
                            <ul class="project__tech">
                                <li>OpenCode</li>
                                <li>Claude Code</li>
                                <li>GitHub Copilot</li>
                                <li>Agent Workflows</li>
                                <li>MCP</li>
                                <li>Jest</li>
                                <li>Playwright</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="experience" class="section">
            <span class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">Experience</span>
